+# S1P — contract
+
+**Twilio SendGrid non-production provider validation.**
+Against **ACOS Operating Spine v1.3**, package issue **v1.3.7** (unchanged by this slice).
+Baseline `d897833` (S1O, corrected in place). Branch
+`feature/s1o-provider-selection-audit-boundary`.
+
+---
+
+## 1. What this slice is for
+
+S1O selected Twilio SendGrid and emitted
+`READY_TO_PROVISION_TWILIO_SENDGRID_NONPRODUCTION_TEST_CREDENTIALS`, which means the
+repository was **locally** ready for provisioning and nothing more.
+
+S1P is the slice that builds everything a real non-production run needs, and takes the run
+itself as far as it can truthfully go.
+
+**IT DID NOT GO FAR.** No SendGrid credential exists in this repository or its environment,
+and the signed class-3 and class-5 records a run needs have not been released. So S1P is the
+REPOSITORY half in full and the PROVIDER half not at all, and the two are reported separately
+throughout.
+
+---
+
+## 2. What v1.3.7 already decided, and S1P did not reopen
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| the provider | Twilio SendGrid. Postmark not selected, Mailgun unresolved |
+| the evidence path | a dedicated non-production identity with `sandbox_mode = false`. **NOT sandbox mode** — it generates no Email Activity and no Event Webhook event |
+| the credential risk model | signed class 5, three classes, maximum reachable privilege, missing fails closed |
+| the identity binding | signed `credential_id` == resolved credential identity, checked in the credential-holding child, before the provider boundary, on both planes |
+| the audit boundary | its own process, its own source, its own allowlist, its own verifier, three read operations, no expressible write |
+| the six kill points | S1J's, by their existing names and at their existing positions |
+| Option A's limit | fewer than three adapters AND no `MONEY_MOVING` credential |
+
+---
+
+## 3. The boundary S1P had to choose, and why
+
+**A REAL VENDOR CLIENT HAD NOWHERE ACCEPTED TO LIVE.**
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| under `src/` | three accepted suites forbid it: no vendor name, no adapter implementation, no real transport. S1M declined to widen them because it "adds nothing which needs the width" |
+| under `tests/` | `§18` reserves `TEST_ONLY` for a "test synthetic provider", and a client that reaches `api.sendgrid.com` is not one. It would put the first real external-write site in the scope EXCLUDED from the production perimeter count |
+
+So S1P adds a fourth perimeter root, **`validation/`**, scanned at **PRODUCTION** scope. Send
+sites carry `PERIMETER_AUTHORISED(authorisation_ref)`; audit read sites carry
+`PERIMETER_EXEMPT(audit_plane_read_only, 48-3-6)`; the operator-invoked capability probes carry
+`PERIMETER_EXEMPT(credential_scope_conformance_probe, 36-13)`. Three accepted assertions were
+amended out loud; see `S1P-owner-clarifications.md` `S1P-C2`.
+
+**`src/` IS UNCHANGED IN EVERY PROPERTY THOSE SUITES ASSERT.** `git diff` over `src/` for this
+slice is empty.
+
+---
+
+## 4. What S1P builds
+
+| Component | File | What it is |
+|---|---|---|
+| request mapping | `validation/sendgrid/integration/requestMapping.ts` | the only constructor of a v3 Mail Send body. Refuses sandbox, refuses a non-owner sink, refuses a tag this kernel did not mint |
+| send client | `.../integration/providerClient.ts` | the one vendor HTTP client for sends. One origin constant, one path constant, literal `'POST'`, no retry, no destination parameter |
+| Z2 adapter | `.../integration/adapter.ts` | `sendgrid_email`. Loaded by the ACCEPTED integration child after its eight guards |
+| kill-point adapter | `.../integration/killPointAdapter.ts` | kill point 3, as a DIFFERENT module specifier. `adapter.ts` has no crash branch |
+| non-secret config | `.../integration/nonProductionConfig.ts` | reads sender/sink/label from the deployment document. Has no member the key could occupy |
+| send secret source | `.../integration/secretSource.ts` | refuses `SYNTHETIC_TEST_IDENTITY` and any identity derived from the material |
+| audit read client | `.../audit/providerReadClient.ts` | `GET /v3/messages` and `GET /v3/messages/{id}`. Declares no `sendToProvider*` |
+| Z4 reader | `.../audit/reader.ts` | `twilio_sendgrid`. Exactly three members |
+| audit secret source | `.../audit/secretSource.ts` | its own document, its own locator, same identity discipline |
+| scope probes | `.../harness/scopeProbes.ts` | `§8.7`'s empirical capability measurements, INCLUDING the `36 §13` attempted write. Outside the audit package by construction |
+| observation | `.../harness/observation.ts` | bounded polling. Its deps have a read and no send |
+| kill-point map | `.../harness/killPoints.ts` | the canonical six, with their provider-side expectations |
