+NO PROVIDER CALL WAS MADE.
+```
+
+Exit code **1**.
+
+**FOUR THINGS A REVIEWER SHOULD READ OFF THIS.**
+
+1. **The `CRITICAL` line is the architecture working.** `50 §3f`'s fail-closed bootstrap
+   raised its own incident because this shell has no deployment trust configuration. The
+   harness does not work around it: with no verified bundle there is no signed class-3 and no
+   signed class-5, and the three gates that depend on them refuse.
+
+2. **`ADAPTER_NOT_IN_SIGNED_CATALOGUE` is `S1P-C1`, as a refusal.** Even with a fully
+   provisioned account, that gate would still refuse until an owner-approved release names an
+   email action class and the `sendgrid_email` adapter.
+
+3. **`CREDENTIALS_NOT_DISTINCT` fires on two ABSENCES.** Two unresolved credentials are not
+   "distinct"; treating them as passing would let a run whose credentials both failed clear the
+   one gate that stops the audit plane and the send plane sharing a key.
+
+4. **The evidence bundle was still written**, with `liveRunPerformed: false`, no probes and no
+   kill-point rows. It is a record of a refusal, not provider evidence, and it says so.
